You can read the size of the data received in bytes by reading the `content-length` response header like this:

```javascript
const impit = new Impit({
    browser: 'firefox',
});
const resp = await impit.fetch('https://example.com');

console.log(resp.headers.get('content-length'));
```

If the server doesn't send the header, you'll have to `await` the entire response with the `text` | `json` | `bytes` methods anyway (or read the `response.body` `ReadableStream` instance).

