This is possible using the `Promise.all()` static method - see [MDN docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise/all). 

```typescript
const impit = new Impit();

const start = Date.now();

const [response1, response2] = await Promise.all([
  impit.fetch('http://localhost:3001/delay/1000'),
  impit.fetch('http://localhost:3001/delay/1000')
]);
console.log(await response1.text());
console.log(await response2.text());

console.log(Date.now() - start); // Prints ~1000, as both requests have been processed in parallel.
```

