Thanks for the contribution! After reviewing this, we'd prefer not to add this since it diverges from the standard Fetch API behavior - when `redirect: 'follow'` hits too many redirects, the spec just throws a `TypeError` with no response attached.        
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
For anyone finding this later - both scenarios from the description can be handled in userland using `redirect: 'manual'`:                                                                                                                                                                    

```typescript                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
const impit = new Impit();
let lastResponse;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           
let url = 'https://example.com/redirect';
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    lastResponse = await impit.fetch(url, { redirect: 'manual' });                                                                                                                                                                                          
    const location = lastResponse.headers.get('location');                                                                                                                                                                                                  
    if (!location || !isRedirectStatus(lastResponse.status)) break;
    url = new URL(location, url).toString();                                                                                                                                                                                                                
}     
```                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
This way you can track URLs, handle timeouts per-hop, and stop whenever you want.                                                                                                                                       
   
